        "descriptions": [
          {
            "descriptionType": "Abstract",
            "description": "This is the first official release of AMPGen, a de novo generation pipeline for broad-spectrum antimicrobial peptide (AMP) design.\n\nKey Features:\n\n\n\nGenerative Models: Utilizes EvoDiff-based order-agnostic autoregressive diffusion models for sequence-based and MSA-based AMP generation.\n\nAMP Classifier: XGBoost model trained on >20k labeled peptide sequences using rich physicochemical features (PseKRAAC, QSOrder).\n\nMIC Predictor: LSTM-based regression model to predict the minimum inhibitory concentration (MIC) values against E. coli and S. aureus.\n\n\nHighlights:\n\n\n\nGenerated peptides demonstrated 85.3% experimental success rate (MIC < 200 µg/ml).\n\nAMPGen supports conditional and unconditional generation, classification, and efficacy scoring.\n\n\nThis release includes:\n\n\n\nPreprocessing scripts for dataset generation.\n\nTrained classification and MIC prediction models.\n\nUsage examples and documentation.\n\n\nPlease refer to the README for detailed setup and usage instructions."
          }
        ],
